---
source: crates/chain-syntax/tests/it/bad.rs
expression: "annotate(&text, &parsed.diagnostics)"
---
  1 | chain 2 "Stores"
  2 | strip #1 "Lead"
  3 | producer render #2
  4 | producer render #3
  5 | bus #4 "Loop"
  6 | bus #5 "Out"
  7 | "Room" -> #1
  8 | #1 -> #2
  9 | #2 => "Print"
 10 | -- E216: a second wire stores in "Print"
 11 | #3 => "Print"
    | ^ 11:1: error E216: "Print" gets a second `=>` wire: a lane keeps the result of one wire, and the first is on line 9
 12 | -- E217: the two buses feed each other
 13 | #1 -> #4
 14 | #4 -> #1
    | ^ 14:1: error E217: the wires make a cycle: #1 -> #4 -> #1
 15 | -- fine: a path that does not come back
 16 | #1 -> #5
 17 | #5 -> @"Strings/Bus"
